Keiran wrote:
> [about a stupid death]

Since you've written about YASD I'll hijack your thread to tell about
mine. Hope that makes you feel a bit better. ;-)

Started Slashem a few weeks ago with the intention not to get spoiled
beyond the things I know from NH. Randomly rolled and got: a Hobbit
Healer! Well, not the best choice for a successful PC in a game that
is said to be very hard, I thought. Nevermind, let's go...

Killed three such hobbit healers in a row - I liked the idea to play
a wimp in a rough universe - reminded me the Tolkien story - and thus
continued this combination. After two of these deaths I noticed super
equipment in my inventory (2 times cursed speed boots, and gauntlets
of power once, just to mention a few). But good stuff had always been
an indication of an early death to me.

The fourth, finally, did not have got fancy equipment early. Good.
Promising. Will make me take more care and survive longer. Indeed did
a good job, finished Sokoban (some unknown puzzles), and got The Bag.
Had found altars that gave me the Mirrorbright. Found some Sword of
Justice that I refused using; after all I am some 4 feet tall hobbit
and a long sword is inappropriate. Got also Demonbane. Stupid Gods!
So I stayed with my scalpel. :-)

I skipped some shopping mall (but visited it later), because in one
of the first games some wax golems succeeded to finish me. Made the
mines, Minetown, the end level, and the level beyond the end level.

Strange creatures, Gnolls and other unknown beasties. No idea whether
they are dangerous, and whether you can eat them. Must start from the
roots; see what my pets eat, heavily use my stethoscope to distinguish
wimps from powerful. And collected a lot of just +0 daggers to not let
them come too close too healthy.

Found the portal to Croesus, but also skipped it. There was another
unknown fortress level with many traps; I did not try to enter that
fortress. Made it, according to the final log, down to level 24.

Went up again to do some offering and prepare some potions and scrolls
to get a better weapon than my now +3 scalpel. I got a +3 crysknife.
Fine, I like it. Knife skill at expert, daggers skilled, so was the
healing spell that saved me and my many pets a lot of times from the
unavoidable.

Then started to make mistakes. Ate an unknown creature that gave me
teleportitis. Dumb. I was not in need of any food. And not much later
ate another unknown but interesting sounding creature: an asphynx.

Well, the experienced Slashem player knows what happened. My final
stats were:  St:15 Dx:16 Co:18 In:11 Wi:18 Ch:16
HP:108(108) Pw:57(106) AC:-12 Xp:12/43561  T:35754
Had many resistances, even hallucination resistance! No idea how I
obtained that.

Had speed boots, an unused wand of death (0:8), wand of polymorph,
rings of polymorph and polymorph control, slow digestion, levitation.
A tinning kit, magic marker (0:40), holy water, a +1 ring of gain
intelligence (which I should have put on %-), and a lot more things
that I have not the slightest idea of what use they are: like the
medical kit, though a healer, I never even bothered to apply it.

 From the list of 1128 killed species there were a lot unknown to me,
a gnoll, Ruggo the Gnome King, the Rat King, a Tasmanian devil, a
pit bull, a brownie, a mangler, an asphynx - at least I killed her
*before* she killed me ;-) -, a nupperibo, a tunnel worm, a bloodshot
eye, 2 caterwauls, a gila monster, 2 squealers, 3 platypi, a scramper,
2 cockatoos, just to name a few. With all these fancy sounding new
creatures I continuously had the impression of being hallucinating!

No genocide, no polyobjects, no wishing, changed form (???) 1 time.
Well, not bad for the start, my little Hobbit Healer.

But nevertheless a completely avoidable YASD.

